  "faqA1": "Open the club from the Clubs tab and tap Join. Approval-based clubs ask for a short note; instant-join clubs make you a member right away. Follow the result in Notifications.",
  "@faqA1": {
    "description": "Key faq.a1"
  },
  "faqA2": "Club boards review applications and usually reply within 1–3 days. Check Profile › My clubs › Pending to update your note or cancel the request.",
  "@faqA2": {
    "description": "Key faq.a2"
  },
  "faqA3": "Raise screen brightness and open the ticket full screen. If it still fails, read the code under the QR to the staff; it can be entered manually.",
  "@faqA3": {
    "description": "Key faq.a3"
  },
  "faqA4": "In Settings › Notification preferences, make sure the system permission is on and the relevant types are not muted. Per-club muting also blocks notifications.",
  "@faqA4": {
    "description": "Key faq.a4"
  },
  "faqA5": "Follow Settings › Delete account. If you are a club president, transfer the presidency first. Your posts and comments are anonymised; memberships and tickets are deleted.",
  "@faqA5": {
    "description": "Key faq.a5"
  },
  "faqA6": "Clubs are added by campus administration. Your advisor or president can ask the Health, Culture and Sports office to add the club.",
  "@faqA6": {
    "description": "Key faq.a6"
  },
  "faqA7": "Your university email identifies your account and cannot be changed. If you mistyped it during verification, use Change email on that screen.",
  "@faqA7": {
    "description": "Key faq.a7"
  },
  "faqA8": "Use the ⋯ menu on a post, comment, user or club and choose Report, then pick a reason. Campus administration reviews it and notifies you of the result.",
  "@faqA8": {
    "description": "Key faq.a8"
  },
